        {
            "id": "048decda-d2eb-49e3-a484-1068bf620749",
            "build_id": "4ee8f038-7bf0-4d2c-8c48-baf90fe24ce8",
            "round_number": 3,
            "cash_earned": 0,
            "created_at": "2025-09-05T15:41:10.236339+00:00",
            "notes": "In round 3, the power I choose is [Packstacker](item_87b99cde-3089-42fd-86bc-6e1ebf3fe422). This power will increase the additional healing the repair packs can do with [Optimizer](item_13d41c37-8f79-4435-9d81-c9599955f6a8) as it increases the duration of your repair packs and therefore increases the duration that you get the additonal 10% healing on. This will also mean that the self-healing you get from Optimizer will also be extended.\n\nFor items in round 3:\nMust have item:\n- [Lumerico Fusion Drive](item_3da81000-333c-460a-a1a2-09441bfda9c8) - This item is a MUST for Brig. Most of her kit is based on abilities, therefore you can have constant uptime on this item between shield bash, whip shot, and your repair packs. This adds so much extra survivability. \n\nItem choices (you can choose any of these items based on your cash and how the game is playing):\n- [Mitzi's Medicine](item_382d3dbd-63b8-453f-9be3-fefc3600dd24) - This item synergizes perfectly in this build as it provides both AP and CD, which are extremely important for Brig's repair packs. The additional overhealth that the repair packs provide can be really good to put a repair pack on a dive teammate as they go in. It will provide extra survivability to them since you should not be diving with them to provide them healing through inspire. Remember, Brig is NOT a tank. \n- If you don't have quite enough money for Mitzi's Medicine, then I will normally stick with the items from round 2: [Ironclad Exhaust Ports](item_2d085fa5-ace6-4fab-9323-b7a06268bcd0) and [Multi-Tool](item_5ba8d94e-f2f3-44b7-8773-025fc6ed7c56).\n- If you are dealing with a lot of dive, then I will sometimes go [Gloomgauntlet](item_76cb8fe3-3c1f-4769-a1ec-a9c2dc510ba7) this round as it provides incredible survivability in those situations. \n\nIf you have extra money after the items above, buy AP items as these scale your repair pack and inspire healing.",
